Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btqca: fall back to request_firmware() when direct load fails

Older trees sometimes call request_firmware_direct(), which bypasses the
userspace firmware helper. If .zst-only files are present, direct lookup
may return -ENOENT. Add a fallback to request_firmware() so udev/user helper
can serve the blob via sysfs while kernel-side Zstd support is being
backported.

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
@@
 static int qca_request_file(struct hci_dev *hdev, const char *name,
                            const struct firmware **fw)
 {
     int ret;
     ret = request_firmware_direct(fw, name, &hdev->dev);
     if (ret == -ENOENT) {
         bt_dev_warn(hdev, "direct firmware load failed for %s (-2); trying helper", name);
         ret = request_firmware(fw, name, &hdev->dev);
     }
     return ret;
 }

/* Adapt callsites to use qca_request_file() in place of request_firmware_* */
/* NOTE: Apply to TLV and NVM paths in your tree as appropriate. */

